      "writtenOn": "2022-09-14T16:19:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u0027this\u0027 referred to the current CL, and elements referred to data blocks / the type indexable by the SSBO index. I figured that the between-element alignment had to match the initial alignment, it would keep things simple to have UniformManager be the only place responsible for aligning/padding.\n\nMy gut says that consecutive data blocks accessed by ssbo index do not need to have the higher initial alignment required for the buffer binding, so I think your original plan is what we should try.",
      "parentUuid": "7833127e_ae40a7fb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 224,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 224,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "9409546712a04e2e2963ced407519f92a9850c6a",
